1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,335
Two instruction manuals.

2
00:00:02,335 --> 00:00:06,499
One thousand six hundred and twenty-three scanned pages.

3
00:00:06,499 --> 00:00:09,325
And not a single searchable character.

4
00:00:09,325 --> 00:00:12,746
Finding one safety rule could take an evening.

5
00:00:12,746 --> 00:00:15,051
This is the problem PDF Q and A

6
00:00:15,051 --> 00:00:16,390
was built to kill.

7
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:19,559
This is PDF Q and A.

8
00:00:19,559 --> 00:00:22,954
Drop in any PDF, even a thousand-page scanned

9
00:00:22,954 --> 00:00:26,651
manual, and it reads every page, saves everything

10
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:30,272
into a database, and answers your questions with

11
00:00:30,272 --> 00:00:31,932
the exact page number.

12
00:00:31,932 --> 00:00:32,611
No cloud.

13
00:00:32,611 --> 00:00:33,818
No subscription.

14
00:00:33,818 --> 00:00:35,930
It runs on your own machine.

15
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:40,521
Uploading is drag and drop, up to twenty

16
00:00:40,521 --> 00:00:41,561
files at once.

17
00:00:41,561 --> 00:00:44,830
Scanned pages are read locally by Rapid OCR,

18
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:47,504
and you watch every page land in the

19
00:00:47,504 --> 00:00:48,544
database live:

20
00:00:48,544 --> 00:00:51,516
page number, percentage, time remaining.

21
00:00:51,516 --> 00:00:53,670
Nothing leaves your computer.

22
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,094
Now ask.

23
00:00:56,094 --> 00:00:58,676
The answer comes back with its source:

24
00:00:58,676 --> 00:01:01,191
the file name, the page number, and a

25
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:02,006
match score.

26
00:01:02,006 --> 00:01:04,657
Open the sources and you are looking at

27
00:01:04,657 --> 00:01:07,171
the exact passage the database found.

28
00:01:07,171 --> 00:01:09,550
You can verify everything yourself.

29
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:12,673
Here is the pipeline.

30
00:01:12,673 --> 00:01:15,687
The browser talks to an Express server.

31
00:01:15,687 --> 00:01:19,011
A Python worker extracts text with PyMuPDF;

32
00:01:19,011 --> 00:01:21,716
scanned pages go through Rapid OCR.

33
00:01:21,716 --> 00:01:25,348
Prisma writes every page and chunk into SQLite,

34
00:01:25,348 --> 00:01:27,590
with an FTS5 full-text index.

35
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:30,758
A question runs a BM25 search first, then

36
00:01:30,758 --> 00:01:33,850
builds the answer from the top passages.

37
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:36,981
Then the AI chain.

38
00:01:36,981 --> 00:01:40,797
Ollama runs first, entirely on your own machine.

39
00:01:40,797 --> 00:01:44,374
Then GLM, NVIDIA NIM, OpenRouter, and Gemini.

40
00:01:44,374 --> 00:01:47,872
If one provider fails, the next one answers.

41
00:01:47,872 --> 00:01:51,212
And if every provider fails, you still get

42
00:01:51,212 --> 00:01:52,802
the database answer.

43
00:01:52,802 --> 00:01:54,630
The system never stops.

44
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:59,458
Libraries and models, exactly as shipped.

45
00:01:59,458 --> 00:02:01,453
Node twenty and Express.

46
00:02:01,453 --> 00:02:04,446
Prisma seven with the libSQL driver.

47
00:02:04,446 --> 00:02:08,020
SQLite with an FTS5 index and BM25 ranking.

48
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,348
PyMuPDF for text and layout.

49
00:02:10,348 --> 00:02:12,509
Rapid OCR on ONNX Runtime.

50
00:02:12,509 --> 00:02:16,665
Ollama runs Qwen two point five, seven B, locally.

51
00:02:16,665 --> 00:02:19,907
The cloud chain is GLM four point seven

52
00:02:19,907 --> 00:02:25,061
Flash, NVIDIA Nemotron three point five Lightning, OpenRouter,

53
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:26,890
and Gemini Flash Lite.

54
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:31,177
And this film was built the same way.

55
00:02:31,177 --> 00:02:34,515
Brag supplied the storyboard, the music and the

56
00:02:34,515 --> 00:02:35,509
sound effects.

57
00:02:35,509 --> 00:02:39,059
Cinematic Skill drove the camera and the captions.

58
00:02:39,059 --> 00:02:42,041
Voice Studio shaped the voice and the mix.

59
00:02:42,041 --> 00:02:45,521
Omni Voice guided the multilingual speech design.

60
00:02:45,521 --> 00:02:49,000
And Playwright MCP took every real screenshot you

61
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:49,710
have seen.

62
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:53,305
Your data stays yours.

63
00:02:53,305 --> 00:02:56,258
View any page, export to text, CSV or

64
00:02:56,258 --> 00:02:58,891
JSON, delete with a confirmation.

65
00:02:58,891 --> 00:03:01,365
The whole app works on a phone.

66
00:03:01,365 --> 00:03:05,115
And a complete Docker plus EC2 deployment guide

67
00:03:05,115 --> 00:03:07,030
ships in the repository.

68
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:10,185
Setup is one command.

69
00:03:10,185 --> 00:03:11,431
Run one command.

70
00:03:11,431 --> 00:03:13,300
Then drop a PDF and ask.

71
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:16,570
The full guide, the Word documents and the

72
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:18,673
code are in the repository.

73
00:03:18,673 --> 00:03:20,230
Thanks for watching.

